Course.start({"num":23,"unit":5,"slug":"m23-reflexivos","minutes":45,"title":"Los verbos reflexivos","subtitle":"Your daily routine: me levanto, me ducho, me acuesto","lede":"When you do something to yourself, like washing your face or getting dressed, Spanish uses a reflexive verb with a pronoun: *me lavo*, I wash myself.","recap":"In Unit 4 you learned **ir**, three kinds of stem-changing verbs, irregular yo forms, **saber** and **conocer**, and **gustar**.","context":{"title":"Un día en el espacio","place":"Centro Espacial Kennedy, Florida · órbita terrestre","text":"On **October 29, 1998**, the space shuttle *Discovery* launched from Florida. On board was **Pedro Duque**, an engineer from Madrid and the **first Spaniard to travel to space**. Over nine days the crew orbited the Earth 134 times and ran experiments on how the human body works without gravity.\n\nDaily routines in space are strange. There's no shower: astronauts wash with damp towels and special no-rinse shampoo. They brush their teeth and swallow the toothpaste, because there's no sink to spit in. At night, they sleep in sleeping bags strapped to the wall, so they don't float away.\n\nDuque described his day in Spanish like anyone else's: {{Me despierto, me lavo, me visto y empiezo a trabajar.}} The little words **me** show that he does each action to himself."},"learn":[{"title":"Reflexive verbs and their pronouns","text":"A **reflexive verb** has **-se** on the end of its infinitive: *lavar**se***. The **se** changes to match the subject and goes **before** the conjugated verb.","conj":[{"inf":"levantarse","en":"to get up","forms":["**me** levanto","**te** levantas","**se** levanta","**nos** levantamos","**os** levantáis","**se** levantan"],"caption":"The verb part is a regular -ar verb; only the pronoun is new."}],"tip":"Compare: {{Lavo el coche.}} (*I wash the car.*) and {{Me lavo.}} (*I wash myself, I get washed.*)"},{"title":"Words for your routine","text":"Stem changes still happen: *despertarse* (e → ie), *acostarse* (o → ue), *vestirse* (e → i).","flash":[["despertarse (ie)","to wake up"],["levantarse","to get up"],["ducharse","to shower"],["bañarse","to take a bath"],["lavarse la cara","to wash your face"],["cepillarse los dientes","to brush your teeth"],["peinarse","to comb your hair"],["vestirse (i)","to get dressed"],["ponerse la ropa","to put on clothes"],["maquillarse","to put on makeup"],["afeitarse","to shave"],["acostarse (ue)","to go to bed"],["dormirse (ue)","to fall asleep"]],"examples":[["Me despierto a las seis.","I wake up at six."],["Mi hermano se ducha por la noche.","My brother showers at night."],["Nos acostamos a las diez.","We go to bed at ten."]]},{"title":"Where the pronoun goes","text":"- **Before** a conjugated verb: {{Me ducho.}} {{No me ducho.}}\n- **Attached** to an infinitive: {{Voy a ducharme.}} You can also put it before *ir*: {{Me voy a duchar.}} Both are correct.\n- With **body parts and clothes**, Spanish uses *the*, not *my*, because the pronoun already shows whose: {{Me lavo las manos.}} (*I wash my hands.*)","tip":"Sequence words help tell a routine: **primero** (first), **luego** (then), **después** (after that), **finalmente** (finally)."}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"conj","title":"Conjugate with the pronoun","intro":"Write each form **with its pronoun** (for example *me ducho*).","pick":2,"verbs":[{"inf":"ducharse","en":"to shower","forms":["me ducho","te duchas","se ducha","nos duchamos","os ducháis","se duchan"]},{"inf":"acostarse","en":"to go to bed (o → ue)","forms":["me acuesto","te acuestas","se acuesta","nos acostamos","os acostáis","se acuestan"]},{"inf":"vestirse","en":"to get dressed (e → i)","forms":["me visto","te vistes","se viste","nos vestimos","os vestís","se visten"]},{"inf":"despertarse","en":"to wake up (e → ie)","forms":["me despierto","te despiertas","se despierta","nos despertamos","os despertáis","se despiertan"]}],"hints":["Pronouns: **me, te, se, nos, os, se**.","Stem changes happen inside the boot, as usual: *me acuesto* but *nos acostamos*."]},{"id":"t2","type":"sort","title":"¿Por la mañana o por la noche?","intro":"When do you usually do each thing?","cats":["por la mañana","por la noche"],"speak":true,"items":[["Me despierto.",0],["Me levanto.",0],["Me visto para la escuela.",0],["Me peino.",0],["Me pongo el pijama.",1],["Me acuesto.",1],["Me duermo.",1],["Me quito los zapatos.",1]],"hints":["*Quitarse* means *to take off* (the opposite of *ponerse*)."]},{"id":"t3","type":"select","title":"Choose the pronoun","intro":"Choose the reflexive pronoun that matches the subject.","items":[{"s":"Yo {me|te|se} levanto a las seis."},{"s":"Mis padres {se|nos|me} acuestan tarde."},{"s":"¿Tú {te|se|me} duchas por la mañana?"},{"s":"Nosotros {nos|se|os} vestimos rápido."},{"s":"Mi hermana {se|te|me} maquilla."},{"s":"Vosotros {os|nos|se} despertáis temprano."},{"s":"Voy a {lavarme|lavarse|lavarte} la cara.","why":"*Voy* = yo, so **lavarme**."},{"s":"Me cepillo {los|mis|mi} dientes.","why":"Body parts use *the*: **los dientes**."}],"hints":["**me** (yo) · **te** (tú) · **se** (él, ella, usted, ellos, ustedes) · **nos** (nosotros) · **os** (vosotros)."]},{"id":"t4","type":"cloze","title":"Mi rutina","intro":"Write the pronoun and the verb form for each verb in parentheses.","items":["Yo [me] [despierto] ((despertarse)) a las seis.","Luego [me] [ducho] ((ducharse)).","Mi hermano [se] [levanta] ((levantarse)) a las siete.","Nosotros [nos] [vestimos] ((vestirse)) para la escuela.","Mis padres [se] [acuestan] ((acostarse)) a las once.","¿A qué hora [te] [duermes] ((dormirse)) tú?"],"hints":["Pronoun first, then the conjugated verb.","Remember the stem changes: *despierto, acuestan, duermes, vestimos* (nosotros is outside the boot)."]},{"id":"t5","type":"listen","title":"La rutina de un astronauta","intro":"Listen to an astronaut's routine and answer.","questions":[{"say":"En el espacio me despierto a las seis y me lavo con una toalla mojada.","q":"How does the astronaut wash?","choices":[["with a damp towel",true],["in the shower",false],["in a bathtub",false],["they don't wash",false]]},{"say":"Me cepillo los dientes, pero no hay lavabo, así que trago la pasta.","q":"What happens to the toothpaste?","choices":[["They swallow it.",true],["They spit it into a sink.",false],["They don't use toothpaste.",false],["It floats away.",false]]},{"say":"Por la noche me acuesto en un saco de dormir en la pared.","q":"Where does the astronaut sleep?","choices":[["in a sleeping bag on the wall",true],["in a bed",false],["on the floor",false],["in a chair",false]]},{"say":"Mis compañeros se duermen muy rápido, pero yo no.","q":"Who falls asleep quickly?","choices":[["the speaker's crewmates",true],["the speaker",false],["everyone",false],["no one",false]]}],"hints":["Tap 🐢 to hear it slowly."]},{"id":"t6","type":"errors","title":"Fix the mistakes","intro":"Tap the wrong word, then type the correct one.","items":[{"s":"Me lavo mis manos.","bad":"mis","fix":"las","why":"Body parts use *the*."},{"s":"Nosotros se duchamos por la mañana.","bad":"se","fix":"nos"},{"s":"Ella se acosta a las diez.","bad":"acosta","fix":"acuesta"},{"s":"Voy a ducharse ahora.","bad":"ducharse","fix":"ducharme"},{"s":"Mi hermano me levanta tarde.","bad":"me","fix":"se","why":"*He* gets *himself* up: **se**."}],"hints":["Check that the pronoun matches the subject."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say your routine","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"Primero me despierto, luego me ducho y después me visto."},{"s":"Por la noche me cepillo los dientes y me acuesto."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Mi rutina diaria","prompt":"Describe a normal school day from morning to night in **at least 6 sentences**. Use at least **five reflexive verbs**, at least **two times** (*a las…*), and sequence words like *primero, luego, después, finalmente*.","model":"{{Primero me despierto a las seis y media.}} {{Luego me levanto y me ducho.}} {{Después me visto y me peino.}} {{Salgo de casa a las siete y cuarto.}} {{Por la noche me cepillo los dientes.}} {{Finalmente me acuesto a las diez y me duermo rápido.}}","placeholder":"Primero me despierto…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 6 sentences","sentences":6},{"t":"Five reflexive verbs (*me…, te…, se…*)","re":"\\b(me|te|se|nos|os)\\s+(despierto|despiertas|despierta|despertamos|despiertan|levanto|levantas|levanta|levantamos|levantan|ducho|duchas|ducha|duchamos|duchan|baño|bañas|baña|bañamos|bañan|lavo|lavas|lava|lavamos|lavan|cepillo|cepillas|cepilla|cepillamos|cepillan|peino|peinas|peina|peinamos|peinan|visto|vistes|viste|vestimos|visten|pongo|pones|pone|ponemos|ponen|maquillo|maquilla|maquillan|afeito|afeita|afeitan|acuesto|acuestas|acuesta|acostamos|acuestan|duermo|duermes|duerme|dormimos|duermen|quito|quita|quitan|relajo|relaja)\\b","min":5},{"t":"Two times (*a las…*)","re":"\\ba\\s+las?\\s+\\p{L}+","min":2},{"t":"Two sequence words","any":["primero","luego","después","finalmente","por fin","entonces","más tarde"],"min":2}]},"reflect":{"q":"From space, Pedro Duque could see the whole Earth while still brushing his teeth like anyone else. St. Ignatius suggested ending each day by looking back over it, an *Examen*. Look back over yesterday's routine. What's one ordinary moment that turned out to be a gift?","placeholder":"One ordinary moment yesterday that was a gift…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"translate","title":"Challenge: translate","items":[{"en":"I get up at seven.","es":["[yo] me levanto a las siete"]},{"en":"She brushes her teeth.","es":["[ella] se cepilla los dientes","[ella] se lava los dientes"]},{"en":"We're going to go to bed.","es":["[nosotros] vamos a acostarnos","[nosotros] nos vamos a acostar","nosotras vamos a acostarnos","nosotras nos vamos a acostar"]},{"en":"Do you (tú) shower in the morning?","es":["¿[tú] te duchas por la mañana?","¿[tú] te bañas por la mañana?"]}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** In Spain, many people still take a **siesta**, a short rest after lunch, especially in summer. Some shops close from about 2 to 5 p.m. and then stay open until 8 or 9 at night.","unitTitle":"Mi casa y mi rutina","code":"ODk5MS1FVVFVRA==","prev":"m22-gustar.html","next":"m24-progresivo.html"});
